Add risks and spike plan

Deliverable 6. The risk register with mitigations and, for each risk,
which spike tests it. Notes that R11, R18 and R19 are one theme: an
interruption becomes a wrong outcome instead of a continuation, which
was the prototype's defining failure.

Four spikes. Spike 1 is the brief's spike: an interpreter workflow
that survives a worker crash and applies a mid-run re-plan, with six
failure injections and six exit criteria. Its measurements include
history size at each continue-as-new, which is what closes brief Q6.
Spike 2 is one real ticket run against real providers. Spike 3 is
concurrent tickets in one repository. W0 is the Windows agent runtime
question, independent and gating Windows work.

Adds the dependency order, what the plan deliberately does not cover,
and five open questions including how long the Spike 1 plan should be
and whether failure injection should kill the process or simulate it.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
